   "unmapped": [
    "Evolving observations: at each round the learner observes feedback losses ell_tau^(t) in [0,1]^K for all past rounds tau <= t, chosen by an oblivious adversary, which may differ arbitrarily from the true losses and retroactively override earlier observations (generalizes delayed, corrupted, composite feedback)",
    "The learner knows an upper bound D_bar on the total feedback inaccuracy D (for the tuned corollary)"
   ],
   "definition_quote": "An oblivious adversary chooses ahead of time not only the true loss $\\ell_t \\in [0,1]^K$ for round $t$, but also the \\emph{feedback loss} $\\ell_\\tau^{(t)}\\in [0,1]^K$, which represents the new observation regarding the actions taken previously at any step $\\tau\\leq t$, overriding any previous observations. ... the full information setting, where after step $t$ the agent observes all the feedback losses $\\ell_\\tau^{(t)}$ for all $\\tau\\leq t$."
  },
